Priya,

Following up on the April 12 false alarm. That was triggered by:
- A passing raccoon triggering cam_driveway_02 at 03:20
- A corresponding humidity spike (58%) from a neighbour's sprinkler system
  causing momentary cross-reading on our basement sensor

Neither required any action. No unknown devices were involved.

Lessons learned:
1. Humidity spikes below 80% are likely environmental false positives
2. Camera alerts without confirmed face match can be deprioritised
3. Correlation with lock events (no entry = lower urgency)

The current incident (if there is one) should be triaged with these
baselines in mind. Key differentiator: unknown device on LAN + confirmed
face match together raises urgency significantly.

Archive reference: incident-2026-04-12 in the archive/ directory.

— David
